Reading through the candidate file to trace each system's wiring.

**Worksheet**

F1: SeededRandom class; `game.rng.next()` used in genMap/genPeople/fireEvent/spawnCaravan; no Math.random found; endTurn() runs 9 fixed steps. Score 2.

F2: 8x8 grid genMap(); terrain from seeded rng; canBuild checks `tile.terrain !== building.terrain`; adjacency "Bonus" text in showTileTooltip is cosmetic only, never applied to output_mult in endTurn(). Score 1.

F3: storage_caps enforced with overflow log/cap in production loop; but FORGE has `production: []` (consumes ore/power, makes nothing), no real ore->metal or multi-step chain functions. Score 1.

F4: people[] individual records (skill, fatigue, morale, job, experience); worker.skill/worker.fatigue read directly in endTurn() production formula. Score 2.

F5: food_need/water_need consumption; shortage reduces p.morale; `worker.morale<50` cuts output_mult; decay is gradual (-5/turn), events/research restore morale — not instant loss. Score 2.

F6: 8 RESEARCH_TREE nodes; prereqs enforced in queueResearch(); costs deducted; but water-retention (water_cap_mult) and ore-refining (ore_to_metal_mult) effects are defined and never read anywhere. Score 1.

F7: 10 events in fireEvent(); selection `available[Math.floor(rng()*available.length)]` is uniform, not weighted; 10 events have 2 choices with distinct state effects; events_cooldown[name]=turn+10 enforced. Score 1.

F8: caravan_prices reads `this.resources[item]/storage_caps[item]`; caravan_inventory limited per spawn; tradeWith() handles both buy/sell branches. Score 2.

F9: storm_severity grows +0.5/turn, storm_dmg scales with it; storm-shelter research halves damage; repair spends 5 parts/building; but production loop never checks `building.health`, so damaged buildings produce at full rate. Score 1.

F10: serializeState()/hashState() exist only for devRunTests/devBenchmark; no player-facing export/import UI, textarea, or paste-parse anywhere. Score 0.

F11: win `people.length>=12 && turn>=60`, lose `people.length===0`, both reachable in endTurn(); score computed from pop/research/resources/turn; endGameModal renders summary. Score 2.

F12: switchTab() wires tabs; log entries carry `entry.turn`; showTileTooltip explains terrain/health/adjacency/buildable; keydown listener for Space/Digit1-5; `@media max-width:600px` layout rules. Score 2.

F13: devRunTests asserts real invariants (resource caps, skill 1-5, fatigue 0-100, health 0-100, research prereqs); devBenchmark spins up headless `sim`, runs 200 endTurn() calls, prints hashState(). Score 2.

G1: `research_done['better-farming']`/`advanced-parts`/`research-lab'` checked directly in production loop each turn, multiplying real output; but effect() objects unused, water-retention/ore-refining branches dead. Score 3.

G2: food/water shortage -> `p.morale -= 10*(1-morale/100)` -> `if(worker.morale<50) output_mult*=0.7` each turn in endTurn(). Score 3.

G3: storm damages `buildings[idx].health`; repair spends 5 parts and restores health; but production loop never reads building.health, so output loss link is absent (rubric caps at 1). Score 1.

G4: `caravan_prices[item]` computed from `this.resources[item]/storage_caps[item]` plus rng jitter at each caravan spawn, shown in trade UI. Score 4.

G5: Settler Arrival choice pushes new colonist into `this.people` vs no-op; Equipment Breakdown choice changes `storm_severity` by -5 vs +2 — both durable state writes, not just logs. Score 4.

